{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.StokesDTBPSBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesDTBPSBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.StokesQZeroDTCount"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.aomega_fourOne_dt_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.aomega_fourOne_dt_count","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesDTBPSBridge.lean#L102-L117","doc":"**`A_ω(4₁) = 3` as a BPS/DT count, conditional on `StokesDTBPSBridge`.**\n\nGiven the bridge, the figure-eight Stokes constant — pinned to `3` by the\nbridge-independent certified `q → 0` datum (`fourOne_stokes_datum`, hypothesis\n`hStokes`) — equals the BPS degeneracy `bpsDim` of `T[4₁]`. Hence the observable\n`A_ω` of the figure-eight **is** a BPS/DT count and equals `3`.\n\n*Derivation, through the bridge:* `bpsDim = dtInvariant` (GPPV, `dt_eq_bps`)\n`= stokesConstant` (GGM Conj 3(d), `stokes_eq_dt`) `= 3` (`hStokes`). The class\nsupplies the two identifications; the value `3` comes from the certified Stokes\ncomputation, not from any class field — the §3b-cond non-degeneracy requirement. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:aomega-fourone-dt-count","label":"thm:aomega-fourone-dt-count","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/aomega-fourone-dt-count.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.fourOne_stokes_datum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.fourOne_stokes_datum","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesDTBPSBridge.lean#L93-L100","doc":"The certified, **bridge-independent** figure-eight Stokes datum that feeds the\nconditional theorem: the GGM eq-(60) `q → 0` off-diagonal of the `4₁` Stokes matrix\nis `3`. Proved unconditionally (decidable integer matrix algebra from the certified\nGGM/DGG `q`-series `W₋₁(0)`) in `StokesQZeroDTCount`; re-exposed here as the named\ninput value `3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesDTBPSBridge.dt_eq_bps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesDTBPSBridge.dt_eq_bps","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesDTBPSBridge.lean#L91-L91","doc":"**GPPV `1701.06567` (with Gaiotto–Moore–Neitzke):** the Donaldson–Thomas\ninvariant is a BPS degeneracy — the dimension of the BPS Hilbert space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesDTBPSBridge.stokes_eq_dt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesDTBPSBridge.stokes_eq_dt","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesDTBPSBridge.lean#L88-L88","doc":"**GGM peacock `2012.00062` Conjecture 3(d):** the resurgent Stokes constant\nis the Donaldson–Thomas invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesDTBPSBridge.bpsDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesDTBPSBridge.bpsDim","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesDTBPSBridge.lean#L85-L85","doc":"Graded dimension of the GPPV BPS Hilbert space of `T[K]`, geometric sector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesDTBPSBridge.dtInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesDTBPSBridge.dtInvariant","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesDTBPSBridge.lean#L83-L83","doc":"Donaldson–Thomas / motivic invariant of the `q`-difference structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesDTBPSBridge.stokesConstant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesDTBPSBridge.stokesConstant","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesDTBPSBridge.lean#L81-L81","doc":"Resurgent Stokes constant of the state integral, geometric Borel ray. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesDTBPSBridge.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesDTBPSBridge.mk","kind":"ctor","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesDTBPSBridge.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesDTBPSBridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesDTBPSBridge","kind":"class","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesDTBPSBridge.lean#L61-L91","doc":"**Adopted conjecture — the closed-sector resurgent-Stokes = DT/BPS bridge.**\n\nFor a hyperbolic knot `K`, three integer invariants of `S³ ∖ K` / `T[K]` are\nconjecturally identified (GGM peacock Conjecture 3(d) + GPPV):\n\n* `stokesConstant K` — the resurgent Stokes constant of the state integral\n  `Z(S³ ∖ K)` on the distinguished (geometric Borel) ray;\n* `dtInvariant K` — the Donaldson–Thomas / Kontsevich–Soibelman invariant of the\n  associated `q`-difference / stability structure;\n* `bpsDim K` — the graded dimension of the GPPV BPS Hilbert space of `T[K]` in\n  the geometric sector.\n\nThe two class fields are the conjecture's *content* (its inputs). There is **no**\nfield asserting any particular value of any of these integers — in particular no\n`A_ω = 3` field; that value is *derived* downstream, only for `4₁`, from the\nbridge-independent certified Stokes datum. An instance of this class is the\nconjecture holding; none is provided (the general conjecture is open — it is a\ntheorem for `4₁`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:stokes-dt-bps-bridge","label":"conj:stokes-dt-bps-bridge","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/stokes-dt-bps-bridge.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}